{"text": "seventeen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">seventene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">seofont\u012bene</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*sebuntehun</i>. Cognate with Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">zeventien</i>, West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">santjin</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">siebzehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">sytten</i>.\nEquivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">seven</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["UK, US", "/\u02c8s\u025bv.\u0259n.ti\u02d0n/"], ["UK, US", "/\u02ccs\u025bv.\u0259n\u02c8ti\u02d0n/"]]}